# Building Atrinik server

Install CMake 3.21 or newer, Ninja, a C17 compiler, Flex, MiniUPnPc,
libcurl, OpenSSL, zlib, libgd, Python development headers, and Check. Then run:

```sh
python3 tools/dependencies.py sync
cmake --preset linux-debug
cmake --build --preset linux-debug
ctest --preset linux-debug
```

The Classic protocol must be available from the sibling `protocol/` tree, the
packaged `dependencies/protocol` tree, or CMake's
`FETCHCONTENT_SOURCE_DIR_ATRINIK_PROTOCOL` override. This keeps the server and
its evolving wire contract on the same repository revision. The first
configure downloads the exact libatrinik source release recorded in
`cmake/dependencies.lock.json` and verifies its SHA-256 digest. Runtime content
and server resources are installed from the release archives recorded in
`dependencies.lock.json`. Use `FETCHCONTENT_SOURCE_DIR_LIBATRINIK` for
coordinated local work. Independently pinned third-party sources such as
libpcpnatpmp retain their checksum-verified FetchContent fallback; use
`FETCHCONTENT_SOURCE_DIR_LIBPCPNATPMP` to supply an existing local source tree.
